We need to actually call tools. Let's call search_template_catalog_by_criteria for amide formation.


{
    "tool_name": "search_template_catalog_by_criteria",
    "arguments": {
        "molecule_smiles": "COc1cccc(NC(=O)c2nnn(Cc3ccc(CN4CC(F)C4)cc3)c2N)c1",
        "functional_groups_broken": ["acyl chloride", "amine"],
        "functional_groups_formed": ["amide"],
        "limit": 5
    }
}

No template found with those criteria. Maybe we can search for generic amide bond cleavage: functional_groups_broken: ["amide"]? Actually forward reaction breaking amide? In retrosynthesis, we break amide bond, so forward reaction forms amide. So broken groups in forward are "acyl chloride" and "primary amine". That didn't return. Could be template uses "alkyl halide" and "amine". Let's search without specifying broken groups, just formed amide.


{
    "tool_name": "search_template_catalog_by_criteria",
    "arguments": {
        "molecule_smiles": "COc1cccc(NC(=O)c2nnn(Cc3ccc(CN4CC(F)C4)cc3)c2N)c1",
        "functional_groups_formed": ["amide"],
        "limit": 10
    }
}
